{
 "_doc": "T2 dialect exclusions (M12 C07, #765): Octave test blocks whose expected behaviour differs from documented MATLAB behaviour. OpenMATLAB follows MATLAB; each block listed here is reported as category toolbox:octave-only, key dialect:<reason> and is outside the T2 rate (never a pass). Only block ids, sha256 hashes and our own reasons are stored: no Octave test source or expected values. An entry applies only while the block's hash matches.",
 "reasons": {
  "interp1-extrap": "MATLAB interp1 extrapolates by default for 'pchip', 'cubic' (= pchip), 'spline' and 'makima' (documented: https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/interp1.html, extrapolation argument); Octave returns NA/NaN out of range.",
  "median-class": "MATLAB median returns natively in the class of A and has no outtype argument (documented: https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/double.median.html); Octave's 'default' outtype returns double for integer and logical input.",
  "var-dim-past-ndims": "MATLAB var returns an array of zeros the same size as A when dim > ndims(A) (documented: https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/double.var.html, dim argument); Octave returns NaN for non-finite elements.",
  "octave-identifier": "The block asserts an Octave-namespaced error identifier ('Octave:...'); MATLAB functions raise MATLAB-namespaced identifiers (component:mnemonic, https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/mexception.html), so the assertion cannot hold in MATLAB.",
  "dec2base-integer": "MATLAB dec2base accepts only nonnegative integer values and errors on a fractional part (documented: https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/dec2base.html, D argument); Octave also converts fractional and negative values.",
  "narg-legacy-message": "MATLAB's legacy nargchk/nargoutchk return 'Not enough input arguments.' / 'Too many input arguments.' (identifiers MATLAB:nargchk:*), an empty matrix when valid (documented: https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/nargchk.html); Octave returns lower-case messages, '' and Octave identifiers.",
  "condest-syntax": "MATLAB condest takes a square matrix and an optional block size t only (documented: https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/condest.html); Octave also accepts function handles for A and its inverse.",
  "movmad-method": "MATLAB movmad computes only the median absolute deviation and has no 'method' option (documented name-value arguments: Endpoints, SamplePoints, DataVariables, ReplaceValues; https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/movmad.html); Octave accepts 'method','mean'|'median'."
 },
